isabled by default."," "," `context_width` controls how many prior tokens seed each watermark decision"," and defaults to 4. Larger values make the watermark less robust to","@@ -61,19 +61,21 @@ weaker detectability. See"," When `watermark_config` is set, the Prometheus counter"," `vllm:watermark_requests_total` counts finished requests by `status`:"," ","-- `watermarked`: the request was sampled with the watermark switched on.","+- `watermarked`: watermarking was enabled for the request, including when","+  enforcement overrides an opt-out."," - `skipped`: the request asked for the watermark (omitted or `true`) but could","   not use it, such as `temperature=0` and trace replay requests. A beam search","   request that asks for the watermark runs without it and logs a warning. Its","-  beam steps count as `not_watermarked`, not `skipped`.","+  beam steps count as `not_watermarked`, not `skipped`, when enforcement is off."," - `not_watermarked`: all other finished requests. This includes explicit","   opt-outs, pooling requests, and the internal requests of beam search (one","-  per beam step), generative scoring and language detection.","+  per beam step), generative scoring and language detection, unless enforced."," "," Each finished request has exactly one status, so the sum over `status` equals"," `vllm:request_success_total` on the same instance. Requests that the client"," aborts are in neither counter. The counter does not exist without","-`watermark_config`. With `n > 1`, each sequence counts once. In a","+`watermark_config`. The Rust frontend (`VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1`) does not","+export this counter yet. With `n > 1`, each sequence counts once. In a"," disaggregated prefill/decode deployment, both instances count a request: sum"," over decode instances only. For streaming input, the first input chunk sets"," the status.","@@ -105,6 +107,7 @@ generation.","   transcription, translation, and realtime transcription, which default to","   greedy decoding. Transcription and translation can use a nonzero temperature","   to apply the configured watermark.","+- `top_k=1` cannot embed a watermark, even with enforcement and nonzero temperature."," - Beam search cannot apply a watermark. The first watermarked beam request emits","   a server-side warning and runs without watermarking."," - Trace replay replaces the sampled token and therefore cannot apply a","@@ -116,9 +119,9 @@ generation.","   Restrictive constraints can reduce the statistical evidence available to a","   detector."," - Automatic language detection and generative scoring use unwatermarked","-  auxiliary generations. Language-detection tokens are not part of the returned","-  transcription, and generative scoring returns scores rather than generated","-  text.","+  auxiliary generations unless enforced. Language-detection tokens are not part","+  of the returned transcription, and generative scoring returns scores rather","+  than generated text."," - Speculative decoding has additional requirements and partial-watermarking","   modes described in [Speculative decoding](#speculative-decoding)."," "],"additions":13,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/engine/test_arg_utils.py","lines":["@@ -92,6 +92,13 @@ def test_watermark_config_cli():","     assert config.deduplicate_contexts == \"none\"","     assert config.deduplicate_contexts_max_history == 32"," ","+    args = parser.parse_args(","+        [\"--model\", \"dummy\", \"--watermark-config\", '{\"key\":42,\"enforce\":true}']","+    )","+    config = EngineArgs.from_cli_args(args).create_watermark_config()","+    assert config is not None","+    assert config.enforce is True","+"," "," @pytest.mark.parametrize(","     \"option\","],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/samplers/test_beam_search_online.py","lines":["@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@","     TokensPrompt,"," )"," from vllm import logger as vllm_logger","-from vllm.config import VllmConfig","+from vllm.config import VllmCon